 ○ #14822  gh run view --job --log-failed fails on required shared-workflow metadata 404                          open
 [ Conversation ] 
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 henrymodisett · 2w
 Symptom
 
 gh run view RUN --job JOB --log-failed fails before fetching logs for a completed
 organization-required workflow run:
 
 failed to get run: HTTP 404: Not Found (https://api.github.com/repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/workflows/WORKFLOW_ID)
 
 The same authenticated CLI can read the run metadata and download that job's logs directly. The
 workflow is required by an organization ruleset and originates in a shared workflow repository,
 rather than a workflow file in the consumer checkout.
 
 Repro
 
 1. Configure a ruleset-required workflow from a shared repository and let its run complete for a
    consumer PR.
 2. Obtain the run/job IDs from the PR check URL.
 3. Run gh run view RUN --repo ORG/CONSUMER --job JOB --log-failed; it fails on the consumer
    repository's workflow metadata lookup above.
 4. With the same authentication, gh api repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/runs/RUN succeeds, and gh api
    --allow-escape-sequences repos/ORG/CONSUMER/actions/jobs/JOB/logs > job.log succeeds. In the
    observed case the latter retrieved 81,118 bytes. Escape sequences were captured to a file, not
    printed to the terminal.
 
 The run metadata's workflow_id is the ID in the failing URL, and path is
 1–25 of 97
 j/k scroll · e expand hidden · o open · y copy url · r refresh · esc close
